From e3bdf1337d8bb28a9755ac7732111975221c95c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 19:07:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 51/75] pm: re-run the default-permission grants when ours
 change
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

GmsCore ships with every one of its dangerous permissions denied on any
device whose profile already existed, even though we ship the grants in
/system/etc/default-permissions/default-permissions-fydroid-gms.xml. On
device that is 33 of 33 runtime permissions granted=false, which crash-loops
gms.persistent —

  java.lang.SecurityException: Need android.permission.BLUETOOTH_CONNECT
    permission for AttributionSource@b645bfc6: getAddress
    at android.bluetooth.BluetoothAdapter.getAddress(BluetoothAdapter.java:1534)
    at ...auth.proximity.firstparty.CryptauthDevicesSyncedIntentOperation

— and leaves location dead for every app that goes through Play services.

The file is never read. grantDefaultPermissionExceptions(), the only code
that parses /etc/default-permissions/, is reachable solely from
DefaultPermissionGrantPolicy.grantDefaultPermissions(userId), which
PackageManagerService calls at boot only for a user where
Settings.isPermissionUpgradeNeeded() holds — that is, where

  PackagePartitions.FINGERPRINT + "?pc_version=" + <PermissionController>

differs from the epoch stored per user in the permission apex data
(/data/misc_de/0/apexdata/com.android.permission/runtime-permissions.xml).
PackagePartitions.FINGERPRINT digests the ro.*.build.fingerprint props, and
ours is pinned to fyde/fydroid_rt/<device> by BUILD_FINGERPRINT_* so that
ro.build.fingerprint stays inside the 91-char cap legacy
__system_property_get() enforces (WeChat). Pinning it also froze the epoch:
it no longer moves when the ARC image is rebuilt, the grant pass never runs
again, and a default-permissions file added after a profile was provisioned
is dead weight. Fresh profiles are fine, which is why this went unnoticed.

Mix an epoch of our own into that fingerprint, bumped whenever the
default-permission content we ship changes, so the next boot runs exactly
one more grant pass per user.

pm grant is not a substitute. Nine of the permissions are restricted
(SMS, call log, ACCESS_BACKGROUND_LOCATION, WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE — the
ones flagged APPLY_RESTRICTION); a shell grant on those silently no-ops,
while the exceptions path passes whitelistRestrictedPermissions=true and
allowlists them as part of the grant.

Verified on device (amd64): after the next boot the stored epoch reads
5f18b3cc...?pc_version=330000000?fydroid_default_permissions=1, and
com.google.android.gms goes from 33/33 runtime permissions denied to every
declared one granted with GRANTED_BY_DEFAULT — the nine restricted ones
carrying RESTRICTION_SYSTEM_EXEMPT|RESTRICTION_UPGRADE_EXEMPT, which a
shell grant cannot produce. gms.persistent stopped crash-looping.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I177b707c8393f99192c2fc6611f432945a26536a
---
 .../java/com/android/server/pm/Settings.java   | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/Settings.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/Settings.java
index cfd029346340..57fdfec89fbb 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/Settings.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/Settings.java
@@ -5427,6 +5427,21 @@ public final class Settings implements Watchable, Snappable {
         private static final int UPGRADE_VERSION = -1;
         private static final int INITIAL_VERSION = 0;
 
+        // fydroid: extra epoch mixed into the permission-upgrade fingerprint below.
+        //
+        // ro.build.fingerprint is pinned to fyde/fydroid_rt/<device> (see
+        // BUILD_FINGERPRINT_* in BoardConfigCommon.mk — it has to stay under the
+        // 91-char cap legacy __system_property_get() enforces), so
+        // PackagePartitions.FINGERPRINT no longer moves when the ARC image is
+        // rebuilt. That froze the epoch, and with it DefaultPermissionGrantPolicy:
+        // an already-provisioned profile never re-reads /etc/default-permissions/,
+        // so grants added there after the profile was created stay denied forever
+        // — GmsCore shipped with none of its dangerous permissions granted.
+        //
+        // Bump this whenever the default-permission content we ship changes; that
+        // makes the next boot run exactly one more grant pass per user.
+        private static final int FYDROID_DEFAULT_PERMISSIONS_EPOCH = 1;
+
         private static final Random sRandom = new Random();
 
         private String mExtendedFingerprint;
@@ -5527,7 +5542,8 @@ public final class Settings implements Watchable, Snappable {
         }
 
         private String getExtendedFingerprint(long version) {
-            return PackagePartitions.FINGERPRINT + "?pc_version=" + version;
+            return PackagePartitions.FINGERPRINT + "?pc_version=" + version
+                    + "?fydroid_default_permissions=" + FYDROID_DEFAULT_PERMISSIONS_EPOCH;
         }
 
         private static long uniformRandom(double low, double high) {
-- 
